## The reading

READ {{corpus.subject}}.

Of those documents, **{{corpus.declared}}** declared their own class or authority and
**{{corpus.undeclared}}** declared nothing and are UNCLASSIFIED — of the unclassified,
{{corpus.conferred}} are classed by the place they reside in and the rest by nothing at all.
{{corpus.unreadable}} carry a declaration that cannot be read. UNCLASSIFIED is a state and not a
failure; whether there are too many of them is a budget's question and a budget is the host's
declaration, so no number on this page is compared with anything.

Where a place declares no ceiling, the cap printed for it is `{{corpus.default_ceiling}}` — the
default the authority vocabulary declares. A place may LOWER what its residents claim and may never
RAISE it.
